# Kyral UI standards

Primitives live in `app/globals.css` and `components/ui.tsx`. Use them; don't restyle per page.

## Buttons
- One `btn-liquid` (primary) per view region, for the main action of that region only.
- `btn-ghost` for secondary actions. `btn-text` for low-emphasis actions and links in UI chrome.
- Sizes: default, `btn-sm` (section headers, rows, nav), `btn-lg` (landing and hero CTAs). Never `!py-*` / `!text-*` overrides.
- Destructive actions are quiet (`text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-red-300`) and always `confirm()`.
- Labels are verbs that say what happens: "Withdraw", "Fund & publish", not "Submit" or "OK".
- Pending state replaces the label ("Sending…") and disables the button.

```tsx
// ❌ unrelated actions grouped, ad-hoc sizing
<button className="btn-liquid">Withdraw</button>
<Link href="/upload" className="btn-ghost !py-1.5 !text-xs">Add more data</Link>

// ✅ each action lives with the content it acts on
<Sheet title="Your data" action={<Link href="/upload" className="btn-ghost btn-sm">Add data</Link>}>
```

## Layout
- Group actions with the content they affect. Money actions stay with balances, data actions with data.
- No cards. Content is rows (`divide-hairline`) inside a `Sheet` / `.glass` surface.
- Page header: `text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight` title, one line of `text-zinc-400` context.
- Section header: `Sheet` `title` plus an optional single `action` on the right.
- Section labels use `.eyebrow`; headline numbers use `.num-display`; metadata uses `.chip`.

## States
- Every async view has loading (`SkeletonRows`), empty (one sentence plus the next step), and error states.
- Errors say what happened and what to do, in plain words. Map wallet/RPC errors to friendly text.

## Copy and crypto
- Amounts in dollars via `<Money>`. Don't say USDC, gas, wallet, or tx in patient-facing copy.
- Onchain proof is a small `<VerifyLink>`, never a primary element.

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)
- Interactive elements are `<button>` or `<Link>`, never clickable `<div>`s.
- Text contrast at least 4.5:1 (`text-zinc-500` is the floor on glass); hit targets at least 24px.
- Inputs have a visible `<label>`; toggles expose their state in text or `aria-pressed`.
